From: Yuanyuan Chen <cyyever@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: flush the TLB after CPU page table updates of
 compute VMs

Compute VMs on large-BAR systems update page tables with the CPU. A CPU
update leaves no fence, so amdgpu_vm_tlb_flush() only bumps vm->tlb_seq
and never creates the TLB flush fence. Only gfx command submission
consumes tlb_seq; KFD user queues never do. The KFD map/unmap ioctls flush
explicitly, but DRM_AMDGPU_GEM_VA (used by hipMemMap/hipMemUnmap) does
not, so after an unmap the queues keep the old translation. Remapping the
VA to a new allocation then sends writes to the freed BO while its
clear-on-release runs: the new allocation reads back zeros.

Flush synchronously when there is no fence to wait on, as the OOM
fallback in amdgpu_vm_tlb_fence_create() already does.

Link: https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-systems/issues/11693
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vm.c
@@ -1059,6 +1059,15 @@
 	tlb_cb->vm = vm;
 	if (!fence || !*fence) {
 		amdgpu_vm_tlb_seq_cb(NULL, &tlb_cb->cb);
+		/*
+		 * CPU updates leave no fence for a TLB flush fence to wait on,
+		 * but the update is already visible, so flush right away.
+		 * Users of need_tlb_fence (KFD and user queues) never consume
+		 * tlb_seq and would otherwise keep stale translations.
+		 */
+		if (!params->unlocked && vm->need_tlb_fence)
+			amdgpu_gmc_flush_gpu_tlb_pasid(params->adev, vm->pasid,
+						       2, true, 0);
 		return;
 	}
 
